{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-33750","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50826","text":"TRAAVIIS — Architecture & the road to the environment surface"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50827","marks":["bold"],"text":"Thesis."},{"id":"spn-50828","text":" TRAAVIIS is the local-first toolchain for "},{"id":"spn-50829","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade agent evaluation"},{"id":"spn-50830","text":". Not another coding agent, not a model router, not an RL cloud, not the whole TRVM research workbench. Its core loop is: "},{"id":"spn-50831","marks":["italic"],"text":"freeze the subject → run the evaluation → score explicit evidence → verify → preserve a re-verifiable receipt."},{"id":"spn-50832","text":" TRVM supplies the strongest exact-replay substrate under it; Evidence Residency is its first repository-evidence substrate.  "},{"id":"spn-50833","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write the wall. Run the world. Keep the proof."}]}],"id":"blk-33751","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-33753","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50834","text":"This document describes the product boundary, what ships today, and the road to the environment surface ("},{"id":"spn-50835","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-50836","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-50837","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-50838","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-50839","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-50840","text":"). It supersedes the earlier \"terminal harness engineer\" thesis — that positioning is retired."}]},{"id":"blk-33754","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50841","text":"1. The product boundary"}]},{"id":"blk-33755","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50842","text":"The seams are frozen on purpose. "},{"id":"spn-50843","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-50844","text":" carries "},{"id":"spn-50845","marks":["bold"],"text":"no substrate semantics"},{"id":"spn-50846","text":"; it packages capabilities the layers below already provide, for someone who does not know the internal history of TRVM."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-33757","spans":[{"id":"spn-50847","text":"layer"}]},{"id":"blk-33758","spans":[{"id":"spn-50848","text":"responsibility"}]}],"id":"blk-33756","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-33759","spans":[{"id":"spn-50849","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS"}]},{"id":"blk-33760","spans":[{"id":"spn-50850","text":"the product — CLI, environment SDK, evaluator, packaging, visual workbench"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33761","spans":[{"id":"spn-50851","marks":["bold"],"text":"trvs"}]},{"id":"blk-33762","spans":[{"id":"spn-50852","text":"the command-line interface"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33763","spans":[{"id":"spn-50853","marks":["bold"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-33764","spans":[{"id":"spn-50854","text":"the substrate-neutral assignment and evaluation contract"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33765","spans":[{"id":"spn-50855","marks":["bold"],"text":"WallRiderLang"}]},{"id":"blk-33766","spans":[{"id":"spn-50856","text":"the language for TRVM worlds, actors and world rules"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33767","spans":[{"id":"spn-50857","marks":["bold"],"text":"Forge"}]},{"id":"blk-33768","spans":[{"id":"spn-50858","text":"the compiler, identity and artifact pipeline"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33769","spans":[{"id":"spn-50859","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM"}]},{"id":"blk-33770","spans":[{"id":"spn-50860","text":"the deterministic execution substrate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33771","spans":[{"id":"spn-50861","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spinner Bench"}]},{"id":"blk-33772","spans":[{"id":"spn-50862","text":"the reference workbench and conformance laboratory"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-33773","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50863","text":"Two rules follow directly:"}]},{"id":"blk-33774","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33776","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50864","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spinner Bench is not TRAAVIIS."},{"id":"spn-50865","text":" It remains the place where the"}]}],"id":"blk-33775","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-33777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50866","text":"language/runtime is exercised, visually inspected, and proven. TRAAVIIS "},{"id":"spn-50867","marks":["italic"],"text":"consumes"},{"id":"spn-50868","text":" those capabilities and packages them."}]},{"id":"blk-33778","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33780","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50869","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvs` invents no state semantics."},{"id":"spn-50870","text":" Every command is a thin call over the"}]}],"id":"blk-33779","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-33781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50871","text":"Forge engine's stable public API ("},{"id":"spn-50872","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.engine → forge_api"},{"id":"spn-50873","text":"). Identity, lowering, folding, and verification live below the CLI and are versioned there."}]},{"id":"blk-33782","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50874","text":"2. What is real today"}]},{"id":"blk-33783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50875","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis"},{"id":"spn-50876","text":" is a zero-dependency Python package exposing the "},{"id":"spn-50877","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-50878","text":" command over "},{"id":"spn-50879","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.engine"},{"id":"spn-50880","text":". Seven commands fold real worlds:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-33785","spans":[{"id":"spn-50881","text":"command"}]},{"id":"blk-33786","spans":[{"id":"spn-50882","text":"contract"}]}],"id":"blk-33784","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-33787","spans":[{"id":"spn-50883","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs doctor"}]},{"id":"blk-33788","spans":[{"id":"spn-50884","text":"reports engine dir, API version, "},{"id":"spn-50885","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-50886","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-50887","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-50888","text":"/oracle status"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33789","spans":[{"id":"spn-50889","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs id"}]},{"id":"blk-33790","spans":[{"id":"spn-50890","text":"re-lowers source → "},{"id":"spn-50891","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-50892","text":" (pure identity)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33791","spans":[{"id":"spn-50893","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs inspect"}]},{"id":"blk-33792","spans":[{"id":"spn-50894","text":"lowered actors, edges, resolved static config, diagnostics"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33793","spans":[{"id":"spn-50895","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs run"}]},{"id":"blk-33794","spans":[{"id":"spn-50896","text":"folds the world through "},{"id":"spn-50897","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-50898","text":"; prints the per-epoch film"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33795","spans":[{"id":"spn-50899","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify"}]},{"id":"blk-33796","spans":[{"id":"spn-50900","text":"cross-checks "},{"id":"spn-50901","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-50902","text":" vs native "},{"id":"spn-50903","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-50904","text":" vs the Fixture oracle"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33797","spans":[{"id":"spn-50905","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs replay"}]},{"id":"blk-33798","spans":[{"id":"spn-50906","text":"re-folds and asserts a pinned "},{"id":"spn-50907","marks":["code"],"text":"--expect"},{"id":"spn-50908","text":" id / "},{"id":"spn-50909","marks":["code"],"text":"--film"},{"id":"spn-50910","text":" hash"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33799","spans":[{"id":"spn-50911","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs diff"}]},{"id":"blk-33800","spans":[{"id":"spn-50912","text":"folds two worlds and marks the first divergent epoch"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-33801","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50913","marks":["bold"],"text":"Identity model."},{"id":"spn-50914","text":" Presentation (position, colour, wire curve) never enters the hash; a rotor value or a rewire does. Run inputs (the scenario) are deliberately kept "},{"id":"spn-50915","marks":["italic"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-50916","text":" of the "},{"id":"spn-50917","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-50918","text":" and carried as a separate "},{"id":"spn-50919","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-50920","text":" digest. This is the split that makes an environment content-addressable."}]},{"id":"blk-33802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50921","marks":["bold"],"text":"Verification contract."},{"id":"spn-50922","text":" A film is not asserted — it is "},{"id":"spn-50923","marks":["italic"],"text":"checked by every applicable verifier"},{"id":"spn-50924","text":". The reference reducer ("},{"id":"spn-50925","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-50926","text":"), the compiled native reducer ("},{"id":"spn-50927","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-50928","text":"), and an independent oracle each run where their domain applies and must agree byte-for-byte. Coverage is explicit: a verifier that cannot apply to a world is reported "},{"id":"spn-50929","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-50930","text":", never counted as a pass or a fail. The Golden Spinner agrees 3/3; a bare Blank Spinner is a valid world for "},{"id":"spn-50931","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32"},{"id":"spn-50932","text":" but sits outside the Fixture oracle's domain. Exit codes: "},{"id":"spn-50933","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-50934","text":" agree, "},{"id":"spn-50935","marks":["code"],"text":"1"},{"id":"spn-50936","text":" ran-and-disagreed, "},{"id":"spn-50937","marks":["code"],"text":"2"},{"id":"spn-50938","text":" a verifier was unavailable. That makes any verifying command a fail-closed gate."}]},{"id":"blk-33803","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50939","text":"3. The environment surface (roadmap)"}]},{"id":"blk-33804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50940","text":"The gap between \"a verifiable world\" and \"an environment an agent trains against\" is task/reward/episode lifecycle. The internal contract for that lifecycle is a "},{"id":"spn-50941","marks":["bold"],"text":"neutral Episode Kernel"},{"id":"spn-50942","text":" — public protocols are "},{"id":"spn-50943","marks":["italic"],"text":"adapters"},{"id":"spn-50944","text":" over it, never runtime law. This keeps "},{"id":"spn-50945","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://openreward.ai"}],"text":"Open Reward Standard"},{"id":"spn-50946","text":" or MCP evolution from ever becoming TRVM runtime semantics."}]},{"id":"blk-33805","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Episode Kernel   start · observe · step · reset · finalize   (internal, neutral)\n        ↓\nORS adapter      first / primary public surface  →  trvs serve --ors\nMCP adapter      compatibility (tools/resources/prompts)  →  trvs serve --mcp\nJSONL adapter    local automation / debugging"},{"id":"blk-33806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50947","text":"The kernel carries "},{"id":"spn-50948","marks":["bold"],"text":"no substrate semantics"},{"id":"spn-50949","text":"; each verb is substrate-defined and may be declared "},{"id":"spn-50950","marks":["italic"],"text":"unsupported"},{"id":"spn-50951","text":" rather than faked. "},{"id":"spn-50952","marks":["code"],"text":"start"},{"id":"spn-50953","text":" prepares the frozen subject; "},{"id":"spn-50954","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize"},{"id":"spn-50955","text":" seals the trace and outputs, runs the verifier plan, scores the reward, and emits the episode. "},{"id":"spn-50956","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-50957","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-50958","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-50959","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-50960","marks":["code"],"text":"reset"},{"id":"spn-50961","text":" are supported only where a substrate can honour them — "},{"id":"spn-50962","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency v1 is one-shot and implements only `start → finalize`."},{"id":"spn-50963","text":" For the TRVM profile, "},{"id":"spn-50964","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-50965","text":" is a label-free "},{"id":"spn-50966","marks":["code"],"text":"_digest_domain"},{"id":"spn-50967","text":" projection, "},{"id":"spn-50968","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-50969","text":" extends the epoch-input stream, "},{"id":"spn-50970","marks":["code"],"text":"reset"},{"id":"spn-50971","text":" reconstructs "},{"id":"spn-50972","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-… + scen-…"},{"id":"spn-50973","text":" at epoch 0, and "},{"id":"spn-50974","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize"},{"id":"spn-50975","text":" checks "},{"id":"spn-50976","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32 == oracle"},{"id":"spn-50977","text":"; those are TRVM profile bindings, not kernel law. The ORS wire surface ("},{"id":"spn-50978","marks":["code"],"text":"list_tasks · session · call_tool → reward · finished"},{"id":"spn-50979","text":") and the MCP primitives ("},{"id":"spn-50980","marks":["code"],"text":"tools · resources · prompts"},{"id":"spn-50981","text":") are both "},{"id":"spn-50982","marks":["italic"],"text":"projections"},{"id":"spn-50983","text":" of the same kernel. The kernel owns the semantics; adapters only translate."}]},{"id":"blk-33807","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-50984","text":"3a. The artifact ladder"}]},{"id":"blk-33808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-50985","text":"TRAAVIIS freezes a "},{"id":"spn-50986","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate-neutral"},{"id":"spn-50987","text":" artifact ladder. The lowest rung is the "},{"id":"spn-50988","marks":["italic"],"text":"substrate subject"},{"id":"spn-50989","text":", sealed differently by each substrate; every rung above it is shared, so two researchers never argue about what agreed and what did not:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-33810","spans":[{"id":"spn-50990","text":"id / rung"}]},{"id":"blk-33811","spans":[{"id":"spn-50991","text":"question"}]},{"id":"blk-33812","spans":[{"id":"spn-50992","text":"domain"}]}],"id":"blk-33809","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-33813","spans":[{"id":"spn-50993","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate subject"}]},{"id":"blk-33814","spans":[{"id":"spn-50994","text":"was it the same subject?"}]},{"id":"blk-33815","spans":[{"id":"spn-50995","text":"TRVM: "},{"id":"spn-50996","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-50997","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-50998","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-50999","text":" · Residency: "},{"id":"spn-51000","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33816","spans":[{"id":"spn-51001","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"}]},{"id":"blk-33817","spans":[{"id":"spn-51002","text":"same scoring rubric?"}]},{"id":"blk-33818","spans":[{"id":"spn-51003","text":"declared reward spec"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33819","spans":[{"id":"spn-51004","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"}]},{"id":"blk-33820","spans":[{"id":"spn-51005","text":"same assignment?"}]},{"id":"blk-33821","spans":[{"id":"spn-51006","text":"subject + reward + terminate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33822","spans":[{"id":"spn-51007","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"}]},{"id":"blk-33823","spans":[{"id":"spn-51008","text":"same observable behavior?"}]},{"id":"blk-33824","spans":[{"id":"spn-51009","text":"the recorded observable record"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33825","spans":[{"id":"spn-51010","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"}]},{"id":"blk-33826","spans":[{"id":"spn-51011","text":"same evaluated outcome?"}]},{"id":"blk-33827","spans":[{"id":"spn-51012","text":"trace + rubric → receipt"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33828","spans":[{"id":"spn-51013","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"}]},{"id":"blk-33829","spans":[{"id":"spn-51014","text":"same environment release?"}]},{"id":"blk-33830","spans":[{"id":"spn-51015","text":"subject + tasks + rewards + splits"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33831","spans":[{"id":"spn-51016","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"}]},{"id":"blk-33832","spans":[{"id":"spn-51017","text":"same distributed package?"}]},{"id":"blk-33833","spans":[{"id":"spn-51018","text":"env + presentation + docs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-33834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51019","text":"The shared evaluation constructs ("},{"id":"spn-51020","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-51021","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51022","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-51023","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51024","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-51025","text":", the substrate profile) live in the "},{"id":"spn-51026","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.*"},{"id":"spn-51027","text":" namespace; substrate-specific evidence lives below. "},{"id":"spn-51028","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-51029","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-51030","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-51031","text":" are "},{"id":"spn-51032","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM substrate identities"},{"id":"spn-51033","text":", not universal rungs; "},{"id":"spn-51034","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-51035","text":" is the Residency subject. A "},{"id":"spn-51036","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trace-…`"},{"id":"spn-51037","text":" is the substrate-neutral observable record; a "},{"id":"spn-51038","marks":["bold"],"text":"`film-…`"},{"id":"spn-51039","text":" is the "},{"id":"spn-51040","marks":["italic"],"text":"TRVM case"},{"id":"spn-51041","text":" of a "},{"id":"spn-51042","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-51043","text":" — a deterministic-execution artifact that does not generalize. Forge owns TRVM compilation and identity ("},{"id":"spn-51044","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-51045","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-51046","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-51047","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-51048","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-51049","text":"); TRAAVIIS owns the shared evaluation ladder."}]},{"id":"blk-33835","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51050","text":"Re-scoring the "},{"id":"spn-51051","marks":["italic"],"text":"same"},{"id":"spn-51052","text":" trace under a different rubric changes the "},{"id":"spn-51053","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-51054","text":" receipt but never the "},{"id":"spn-51055","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-51056","text":" — the recorded behavior did not change."}]},{"id":"blk-33836","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51057","text":"Canonical form (what an id is a hash "},{"id":"spn-51058","marks":["italic"],"text":"of"},{"id":"spn-51059","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-33837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51060","text":"Every rung is "},{"id":"spn-51061","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-<sha256(canonical_bytes(document))>"},{"id":"spn-51062","text":", where "},{"id":"spn-51063","marks":["code"],"text":"canonical_bytes"},{"id":"spn-51064","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-51065","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS canonical JSON"},{"id":"spn-51066","text":": UTF-8, object keys sorted, no insignificant whitespace — concretely "},{"id":"spn-51067","marks":["code"],"text":"json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False)"},{"id":"spn-51068","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-33838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51069","text":"This is "},{"id":"spn-51070","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-51071","text":" RFC 8785 (JCS), and the difference is stated here rather than discovered by a reimplementer. It is byte-identical to RFC 8785 over documents whose keys hold no code point at or above U+10000 and whose numbers avoid four bands, but it differs in two ways that are already reachable:"}]},{"id":"blk-33839","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33841","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51072","marks":["bold"],"text":"Numbers."},{"id":"spn-51073","text":" RFC 8785 mandates ECMAScript "},{"id":"spn-51074","marks":["code"],"text":"Number::toString"},{"id":"spn-51075","text":"; Python does not"}]}],"id":"blk-33840","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51076","text":"match it for integral-valued floats below 10²¹ ("},{"id":"spn-51077","marks":["code"],"text":"1.0"},{"id":"spn-51078","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-51079","marks":["code"],"text":"1"},{"id":"spn-51080","text":"), for "},{"id":"spn-51081","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.0"},{"id":"spn-51082","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-51083","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.0"},{"id":"spn-51084","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-51085","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-51086","text":"), across "},{"id":"spn-51087","marks":["code"],"text":"[1e16, 1e21)"},{"id":"spn-51088","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-51089","marks":["code"],"text":"[1e-6, 1e-4)"},{"id":"spn-51090","text":", or on exponent zero-padding ("},{"id":"spn-51091","marks":["code"],"text":"1e-07"},{"id":"spn-51092","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-51093","marks":["code"],"text":"1e-7"},{"id":"spn-51094","text":"). A receipt's "},{"id":"spn-51095","marks":["code"],"text":"reward"},{"id":"spn-51096","text":" is always a float, so a fully-passing episode carries "},{"id":"spn-51097","marks":["code"],"text":"1.0"},{"id":"spn-51098","text":" and is on the diverging side."}]},{"id":"blk-33843","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51099","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key order."},{"id":"spn-51100","text":" RFC 8785 sorts property names by UTF-16 code unit; Python sorts"}]}],"id":"blk-33844","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33846","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51101","text":"by code point. These agree below U+10000 and diverge above it, so a subject repository containing an astral-plane filename orders its "},{"id":"spn-51102","marks":["code"],"text":"files"},{"id":"spn-51103","text":" map differently under the two schemes."}]},{"id":"blk-33847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51104","text":"Nothing enforces the agreeing subset — there is no schema check, key charset check or numeric domain check anywhere on the path. "},{"id":"spn-51105","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_canonical.py"},{"id":"spn-51106","text":" measures all of this against a reference RFC 8785 implementation and pins each divergence with a reproducing value; treat it as the specification of the canonical form until a ruling decides whether to conform and migrate."}]},{"id":"blk-33848","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51107","text":"3b. The bundle — "},{"id":"spn-51108","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.environment.v1"}]},{"id":"blk-33849","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51109","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-51110","text":" separates "},{"id":"spn-51111","marks":["italic"],"text":"what an environment means"},{"id":"spn-51112","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-51113","marks":["italic"],"text":"how it is shipped"},{"id":"spn-51114","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-51115","marks":["bold"],"text":"environment manifest"},{"id":"spn-51116","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-51117","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-51118","text":") fixes the substrate subject, tasks, rewards, action / observation or verifier profiles, and split membership; the outer "},{"id":"spn-51119","marks":["bold"],"text":"package"},{"id":"spn-51120","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-51121","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-51122","text":") carries presentation, docs, and screenshots and may change without moving "},{"id":"spn-51123","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-51124","text":". For the TRVM substrate it layers over the existing "},{"id":"spn-51125","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.bundle.v2"},{"id":"spn-51126","text":" (world + scenarios, already closed), adding "},{"id":"spn-51127","marks":["code"],"text":"{tasks, rewards, splits, profiles}"},{"id":"spn-51128","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-33850","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51129","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-51130","text":" runs against a "},{"id":"spn-51131","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate-profile admission interface"},{"id":"spn-51132","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-51133","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_subject · verify_closure · recompute_subject_identity · reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-51134","text":"), not against "},{"id":"spn-51135","marks":["code"],"text":"world"},{"id":"spn-51136","text":" verbs; each substrate implements it (TRVM re-lowers source → "},{"id":"spn-51137","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-51138","text":"; Residency recomputes snapshot → "},{"id":"spn-51139","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-51140","text":"). Three laws (mirroring the existing Forge bundle discipline):"}]},{"id":"blk-33851","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33853","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51141","marks":["bold"],"text":"self-sufficiency"},{"id":"spn-51142","text":" — the object set is derived from the doc."}]}],"id":"blk-33852","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51143","marks":["bold"],"text":"closure"},{"id":"spn-51144","text":" — the subject re-derives to its declared identity and every task /"}]}],"id":"blk-33854","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33856","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51145","text":"reward / subject reference resolves inside the closure, or import fails loudly."}]},{"id":"blk-33857","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51146","marks":["bold"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-51147","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-51148","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-51149","text":" re-opens and re-verifies the emitted bundle before"}]}],"id":"blk-33858","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33860","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51150","text":"reporting success."}]},{"id":"blk-33861","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51151","marks":["bold"],"text":"Shipped"},{"id":"spn-51152","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-51153","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"},{"id":"spn-51154","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51155","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/pack.py"},{"id":"spn-51156","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51157","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/scaffold.py"},{"id":"spn-51158","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-51159","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-51160","text":" scaffolds and derives nothing — it emits scaffold-level references ("},{"id":"spn-51161","marks":["code"],"text":"reward_spec"},{"id":"spn-51162","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51163","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot_def"},{"id":"spn-51164","text":") precisely so it never asserts a hash it did not compute — and "},{"id":"spn-51165","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-51166","text":" replaces them with recomputed ids. "},{"id":"spn-51167","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-51168","text":" is derived from an explicit identity allowlist ("},{"id":"spn-51169","marks":["code"],"text":"substrate_profile · subject · tasks · rewards · profiles · splits"},{"id":"spn-51170","text":"), so renaming an environment or rewriting its description moves the "},{"id":"spn-51171","marks":["italic"],"text":"package"},{"id":"spn-51172","text":", never "},{"id":"spn-51173","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-51174","text":". Both substrate profiles are implemented; a single-task residency package is emitted as a runnable eval-bundle, closing "},{"id":"spn-51175","marks":["code"],"text":"init → pack → eval-one"},{"id":"spn-51176","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-33862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51177","text":"An episode emits a receipt:"}]},{"id":"blk-33863","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\", \"substrate_profile\": \"trvm.world.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\", \"subject\": { \"world\": \"sem-…\", \"scenario\": \"scen-…\" },\n  \"reward_id\": \"rew-…\", \"trace\": \"film-…\", \"episode_id\": \"episode-…\",\n  \"reward\": 1, \"status\": \"ok\", \"finished\": true,\n  \"verification\": { \"reference\": \"pass\", \"native\": \"pass\", \"oracle\": \"not_applicable\" } }"},{"id":"blk-33864","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51178","text":"For a Residency episode the same receipt carries "},{"id":"spn-51179","marks":["code"],"text":"\"substrate_profile\": \"residency.repository.v1\""},{"id":"spn-51180","text":", a "},{"id":"spn-51181","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-51182","text":" in place of the "},{"id":"spn-51183","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-51184","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-51185","marks":["code"],"text":"citations"},{"id":"spn-51186","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-51187","marks":["code"],"text":"patch"},{"id":"spn-51188","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-51189","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"},{"id":"spn-51190","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-51191","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-51192","text":" verifier fields. Every verifier field is one of "},{"id":"spn-51193","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"},{"id":"spn-51194","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51195","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-51196","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51197","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-51198","text":", or "},{"id":"spn-51199","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-51200","text":" — coverage is never silently dropped, and "},{"id":"spn-51201","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-51202","text":" (substrate unavailable) stays distinct from "},{"id":"spn-51203","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-51204","text":" (the work was wrong)."}]},{"id":"blk-33865","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51205","text":"3c. Evaluation before training"}]},{"id":"blk-33866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51206","text":"The first job is not a trainer, and the first interface is not a batch. It is a one-shot "},{"id":"spn-51207","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvs eval-one task.json --agent-command …`"},{"id":"spn-51208","text":" over a single frozen subject. Batch "},{"id":"spn-51209","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-51210","text":" follows once eval-one is boring. Because every episode is verified and content-addressed, the numbers are reproducible and the traces are re-checkable. Training frameworks drive rollouts "},{"id":"spn-51211","marks":["italic"],"text":"through"},{"id":"spn-51212","text":" the ORS adapter later."}]},{"id":"blk-33867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51213","marks":["bold"],"text":"Shipped"},{"id":"spn-51214","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-51215","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/evalsplit.py"},{"id":"spn-51216","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-51217","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval PKG --split NAME"},{"id":"spn-51218","text":" runs an agent over a split and emits one "},{"id":"spn-51219","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-51220","text":" per task. It adds "},{"id":"spn-51221","marks":["bold"],"text":"no rung to the ladder"},{"id":"spn-51222","text":" — §1 stops at "},{"id":"spn-51223","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-51224","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-51225","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-51226","text":", so a run over a split gets an "},{"id":"spn-51227","marks":["italic"],"text":"index"},{"id":"spn-51228","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-51229","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.evaluation.v1"},{"id":"spn-51230","text":") naming the "},{"id":"spn-51231","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-51232","text":", the split, and the episode ids, and carries no id of its own. The admission order mirrors "},{"id":"spn-51233","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-51234","text":": reopen the package (every id re-derived from the written bytes) → resolve the split → bind the subject tree to its snapshot → "},{"id":"spn-51235","marks":["italic"],"text":"only then"},{"id":"spn-51236","text":" launch anything. A task that fails is recorded as a failed episode and the split continues; a refusal exits 2 rather than reporting a score of zero."}]},{"id":"blk-33868","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51237","marks":["italic"],"text":"Canonical form."},{"id":"spn-51238","text":" An environment is a closed "},{"id":"spn-51239","marks":["bold"],"text":"set"},{"id":"spn-51240","text":" of tasks, rewards and split members (§3), and a set has exactly one written order — so "},{"id":"spn-51241","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-51242","text":" sorts tasks and rewards by their derived ids and split members by task id, and reordering an author's source list moves no identity. Producing that order is not enough: "},{"id":"spn-51243","marks":["code"],"text":"open_package"},{"id":"spn-51244","text":" "},{"id":"spn-51245","marks":["bold"],"text":"re-checks"},{"id":"spn-51246","text":" it, because a hand-built manifest that is internally consistent but unsorted would otherwise reopen cleanly and give one environment as many identities as its task list has permutations. A noncanonical manifest is "},{"id":"spn-51247","marks":["code"],"text":"MANIFEST_NONCANONICAL"},{"id":"spn-51248","text":", checked before the "},{"id":"spn-51249","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-51250","text":" comparison so the failure reads as a malformed "},{"id":"spn-51251","marks":["italic"],"text":"form"},{"id":"spn-51252","text":" rather than a confusing identity mismatch."}]},{"id":"blk-33869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51253","marks":["italic"],"text":"Two outcomes, not one."},{"id":"spn-51254","text":" Each index entry carries "},{"id":"spn-51255","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-51256","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-51257","marks":["code"],"text":"reward"},{"id":"spn-51258","text":" — what the evaluation found — and a separate "},{"id":"spn-51259","marks":["code"],"text":"persistence {requested, status, error}"},{"id":"spn-51260","text":" — whether the evidence the caller asked to keep was kept. Conflating them once let a run report "},{"id":"spn-51261","marks":["code"],"text":"ok"},{"id":"spn-51262","text":" for an episode whose bundle had failed to write: a score with no retained proof, reported as if the proof existed. The totals count both, and the exit code reads them in precedence — persistence failure 2, disagreement 1, otherwise 0. "},{"id":"spn-51263","marks":["code"],"text":"OSError"},{"id":"spn-51264","text":" is caught alongside "},{"id":"spn-51265","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeBundleError"},{"id":"spn-51266","text":" deliberately: a read-only output directory is the most ordinary way retention fails, and it must be a recorded outcome for one task rather than an exception that abandons the rest of the split."}]},{"id":"blk-33870","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51267","text":"3c-bis. Verifier wiring — "},{"id":"spn-51268","marks":["code"],"text":"VerifierRegistryV1"}]},{"id":"blk-33871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51269","text":"Three things that are easy to conflate are kept distinct:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-33873","spans":[{"id":"spn-51270","text":"layer"}]},{"id":"blk-33874","spans":[{"id":"spn-51271","text":"function of"}]},{"id":"blk-33875","spans":[{"id":"spn-51272","text":"where it lives"}]}],"id":"blk-33872","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-33876","spans":[{"id":"spn-51273","text":"declared plan"}]},{"id":"blk-33877","spans":[{"id":"spn-51274","text":"the task alone"}]},{"id":"blk-33878","spans":[{"id":"spn-51275","marks":["code"],"text":"wiring.declared_signals"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33879","spans":[{"id":"spn-51276","text":"available implementations"}]},{"id":"blk-33880","spans":[{"id":"spn-51277","text":"task + runtime/registry"}]},{"id":"blk-33881","spans":[{"id":"spn-51278","marks":["code"],"text":"VerifierRegistryV1"}]}],[{"id":"blk-33882","spans":[{"id":"spn-51279","text":"sealed history"}]},{"id":"blk-33883","spans":[{"id":"spn-51280","text":"what actually answered"}]},{"id":"blk-33884","spans":[{"id":"spn-51281","marks":["code"],"text":"receipt.verifier_versions"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-33885","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51282","text":"The registry is built "},{"id":"spn-51283","marks":["bold"],"text":"once per command"},{"id":"spn-51284","text":" from the engine that command selected, so every task in a split is answered by the same verifiers bound to the same Forge checkout — and "},{"id":"spn-51285","marks":["code"],"text":"real_adapter(forge_api)"},{"id":"spn-51286","text":" takes that engine explicitly rather than independently rediscovering a possibly different one. An unreachable engine leaves "},{"id":"spn-51287","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-51288","text":" declared but unwired, reported as a note; it is never silently dropped and never faked into a "},{"id":"spn-51289","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"},{"id":"spn-51290","text":". Because the versions are sealed into "},{"id":"spn-51291","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-51292","text":", an engine upgrade honestly moves the episode id instead of quietly re-scoring the same one."}]},{"id":"blk-33886","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51293","text":"3c-ter. Test plans — "},{"id":"spn-51294","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.test-plan.v2"}]},{"id":"blk-33887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51295","text":"V2 replaced host-specific "},{"id":"spn-51296","marks":["code"],"text":"argv"},{"id":"spn-51297","text":" with a logical "},{"id":"spn-51298","marks":["code"],"text":"tool"},{"id":"spn-51299","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-51300","marks":["code"],"text":"args"},{"id":"spn-51301","text":" under a named "},{"id":"spn-51302","marks":["code"],"text":"toolchain_profile"},{"id":"spn-51303","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-51304","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-51305","text":" is host-independent and the resolved binary is an execution fact. It further lets each command declare per-phase "},{"id":"spn-51306","marks":["code"],"text":"allowed_exit_codes"},{"id":"spn-51307","text":", both defaulting to "},{"id":"spn-51308","marks":["code"],"text":"[0]"},{"id":"spn-51309","text":" — exactly the V1 rule, so an undeclared plan keeps its old meaning. This is what makes a "},{"id":"spn-51310","marks":["bold"],"text":"repair task"},{"id":"spn-51311","text":" expressible: under a hardcoded baseline-must-exit-0 rule, a task could not require a test that fails before the fix and passes after, which is the ordinary shape of a real bug report. The verdict asymmetry is deliberate — the baseline judges the "},{"id":"spn-51312","marks":["italic"],"text":"fixture"},{"id":"spn-51313","text":" (a miss is "},{"id":"spn-51314","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-51315","text":", the task is inadmissible), the patched run judges the "},{"id":"spn-51316","marks":["italic"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-51317","text":" (a miss is "},{"id":"spn-51318","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-51319","text":") — and every record states the "},{"id":"spn-51320","marks":["code"],"text":"expected_exit_codes"},{"id":"spn-51321","text":" it was judged by, so the evidence names its own rule."}]},{"id":"blk-33888","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51322","text":"3d. Later: verified process rewards"}]},{"id":"blk-33889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51323","text":"Because TRVM films observe each transition, TRAAVIIS can eventually emit intermediate, verifier-grounded rewards (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-51324","marks":["code"],"text":"+0.2 preserved safety invariant"},{"id":"spn-51325","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51326","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.3 duplicated forbidden resource"},{"id":"spn-51327","text":") rather than only a terminal reward. This depends entirely on verifier reliability, so it ships "},{"id":"spn-51328","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-51329","text":" deterministic terminal rewards and complete episodes are solid."}]},{"id":"blk-33890","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51330","text":"4. Sequencing"}]},{"id":"blk-33891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51331","text":"The thesis is "},{"id":"spn-51332","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade environments for evaluating agents"},{"id":"spn-51333","text":". The sequencing builds "},{"id":"spn-51334","marks":["italic"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-51335","text":" end-to-end evaluation environment before widening the platform. Flagship worlds ship in this order:"}]},{"id":"blk-33892","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51336","marks":["bold"],"text":"Golden Spinner → Evidence Residency → Courier → WallRider."}]},{"id":"blk-33893","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51337","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.7-5 (Spinner Bench)"},{"id":"spn-51338","text":" — close the Public Alpha: freeze presentation,"}]}],"id":"blk-33894","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51339","text":"package source, document limits, publish reproducible acceptance. Then freeze Bench feature work. Bench proceeds "},{"id":"spn-51340","marks":["italic"],"text":"independently"},{"id":"spn-51341","text":" and does not block the evaluation surface below."}]},{"id":"blk-33897","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33899","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51342","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.1"},{"id":"spn-51343","text":" — the shared artifact ladder as pure identity functions"}]}],"id":"blk-33898","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51344","text":"("},{"id":"spn-51345","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot_id · finding_id · patch_id · trace_id · reward_id · task_id · episode_id"},{"id":"spn-51346","text":") with mutation-law tests, then "},{"id":"spn-51347","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-51348","text":" over "},{"id":"spn-51349","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency"},{"id":"spn-51350","text":" — an agent inspects a frozen repository, finds a real spec/impl inconsistency, cites evidence, proposes the smallest patch, runs the declared checks, and returns a structured finding + a re-verifiable receipt. Ship Golden Spinner as the first TRVM bundle alongside. See "},{"id":"spn-51351","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_EVIDENCE_RESIDENCY.md"},{"id":"spn-51352","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-33901","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51353","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.2"},{"id":"spn-51354","text":" — the Episode Kernel + "},{"id":"spn-51355","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors"},{"id":"spn-51356","text":"; ship the"}]}],"id":"blk-33902","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51357","marks":["bold"],"text":"Courier"},{"id":"spn-51358","text":"/Factory world so the kernel is exercised by a stateful, long-horizon environment "},{"id":"spn-51359","marks":["italic"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-51360","text":" batch "},{"id":"spn-51361","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-51362","text":" is called complete."}]},{"id":"blk-33905","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33907","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51363","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.3"},{"id":"spn-51364","text":" — batch "},{"id":"spn-51365","marks":["code"],"text":"eval · compare · reports"},{"id":"spn-51366","text":" over the kernel; MCP"}]}],"id":"blk-33906","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51367","text":"adapter."}]},{"id":"blk-33909","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33911","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51368","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.4"},{"id":"spn-51369","text":" — an ORS/TRL example, process-reward hooks, environment"}]}],"id":"blk-33910","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51370","text":"publishing; ship the "},{"id":"spn-51371","marks":["bold"],"text":"WallRider"},{"id":"spn-51372","text":"/Graffiti world."}]},{"id":"blk-33913","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51373","text":"5. What is deliberately not built"}]},{"id":"blk-33914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51374","text":"Model routing · generic sub-agent orchestration · another chat interface · a cloud GPU training service · a giant environment marketplace · a complete game engine · plugin systems before the bundle/session API is stable · a complex interactive REPL · automatic LLM world generation as the core proposition."}]},{"id":"blk-33915","kind":"parag